<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Smart Group lifts half yr shr, div passed.</title>
<headline>Smart Group lifts half yr shr, div passed.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     55.2	  vs 47.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   27.69	 vs 19.74</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   45.65	 vs 31.93</p>
<p>    Tax			 15.98	 vs 11.03</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   9.62	  vs 5.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		  276.87	vs 210.70</p>
<p>Full name: Smart Group Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - In line with company policy, no interim dividend was declared. Directors said although difficult trading conditions would in all probability continue, they expected to show real profit growth for the year.</p>
<p>Shareholders were reminded that a disproportionate share of the annual profit was generated in the first half of the trading year due to the high turnover associated with the festive season.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
